The 60-Second "Holy Trinity" Speedrun Guide
To permanently connect your Drive, you need to generate your own private keys. It takes exactly one minute:

Go to Google Cloud Console: console.cloud.google.com and log in.
Create a Project: Click the dropdown at the top left, click New Project, name it "Engine 6", and click Create.
Enable Drive API: Search for "Google Drive API" in the top search bar, click it, and hit the blue Enable button.
Create the Client ID & Secret: * Go to APIs & Services -> Credentials.
Click + Create Credentials and select OAuth client ID.
(If it asks you to configure a Consent Screen first, click "External", fill out just the required App Name and Email, save, and return to Credentials).
For Application Type, choose Desktop App (or "Web application" with redirect URI https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground).
Copy your Client ID and Client Secret.

Go to Google auth platform > Audience  > Test user > put email id of Gdrive

Also in Google auth platform > Audience > Change to Publish from testing once tested done.

Get the Refresh Token:
Open a new tab to developers.google.com/oauthplayground.
Click the Gear Icon (top right) -> Check Use your own OAuth credentials -> Paste your Client ID and Secret.
On the left, scroll to Drive API v3, select https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.
Click Authorize APIs, sign into your account, and hit Continue.
Click Exchange authorization code for tokens.
Copy the Refresh Token.
Paste all three into Engine 6, click Connect, and watch the light turn green!


